markdown <<MARKDOWN
<h1>Foundations of AI Programming Curriculum Overview</h1>

<p>The <b>Foundations of AI Programming</b> curriculum unit introduces students to programming, algorithms, and ethical computing.</p>

<p>They learn how algorithms solve problems, how to design and debug Python programs with AI tools, and will consider the societal impact of computing.</p>

<div style="background-color: #F7F7FB; padding: 20px; border-radius: 10px; max-width: 800px; margin: 20px auto;">
<h2>Students will:</h2>
<p style="margin: 0 0 10px 0;">• Define, analyze, and improve algorithms using sequence, selection, and iteration.</p>
<p style="margin: 0 0 10px 0;">• Use variables, conditionals, loops, and functions to create, test, and refine modular programs.</p>
<p style="margin: 0 0 10px 0;">• Assess AI technologies for biases and privacy concerns, proposing strategies to mitigate risks.</p>
<p style="margin: 0 0 10px 0;">• Connect programming skills to real-world opportunities in computing and related industries.</p>
<p style="margin: 0;">• Use abstraction, decomposition, and pattern recognition to design and troubleshoot programs effectively.</p>
</div>

<hr>

<h2>Unit Calendar</h2>

<p>Take a quick look at the lessons included in this unit using the calendar tool. This version of the calendar assumes 5 45-minute lessons per week.</p>

<div style="font-family: 'Segoe UI', Tahoma, Geneva, Verdana, sans-serif; max-width: 860px; margin: 0 auto; border-radius: 10px; overflow: hidden; border: 1.5px solid #ACA8EA;">

  <!-- Week 1 -->
  <div style="display: flex; align-items: stretch; border-bottom: 2px solid #fff;">
    <div style="background: #4C42CF; color: #fff; font-weight: 700; font-size: 14px; display: flex; align-items: center; justify-content: center; min-width: 72px; padding: 16px 10px; text-align: center;">
      Week 1
    </div>
    <div style="display: flex; flex: 1; flex-wrap: wrap; background: #E4E2F8; gap: 6px; padding: 10px;">
      <div style="background: #fff; border: 1.5px solid #ACA8EA; border-radius: 6px; padding: 10px; flex: 1 1 120px; min-width: 110px; font-size: 12.5px; color: #1F1976; text-align: center; line-height: 1.4;">
        <span style="display:block; font-size:10px; font-weight:600; color:#4C42CF; margin-bottom:4px; text-transform:uppercase;">Lesson 1</span>
        Computing Careers
      </div>
      <div style="background: #fff; border: 1.5px solid #ACA8EA; border-radius: 6px; padding: 10px; flex: 1 1 120px; min-width: 110px; font-size: 12.5px; color: #1F1976; text-align: center; line-height: 1.4;">
        <span style="display:block; font-size:10px; font-weight:600; color:#4C42CF; margin-bottom:4px; text-transform:uppercase;">Lesson 2</span>
        Computational Thinking
      </div>
      <div style="background: #fff; border: 1.5px solid #ACA8EA; border-radius: 6px; padding: 10px; flex: 1 1 120px; min-width: 110px; font-size: 12.5px; color: #1F1976; text-align: center; line-height: 1.4;">
        <span style="display:block; font-size:10px; font-weight:600; color:#4C42CF; margin-bottom:4px; text-transform:uppercase;">Lesson 3</span>
        Designing Algorithms
      </div>
      <div style="background: #fff; border: 1.5px solid #ACA8EA; border-radius: 6px; padding: 10px; flex: 1 1 120px; min-width: 110px; font-size: 12.5px; color: #1F1976; text-align: center; line-height: 1.4;">
        <span style="display:block; font-size:10px; font-weight:600; color:#4C42CF; margin-bottom:4px; text-transform:uppercase;">Lesson 4</span>
        Variables and Data Flow
      </div>
      <div style="background: #fff; border: 1.5px solid #ACA8EA; border-radius: 6px; padding: 10px; flex: 1 1 120px; min-width: 110px; font-size: 12.5px; color: #1F1976; text-align: center; line-height: 1.4;">
        <span style="display:block; font-size:10px; font-weight:600; color:#4C42CF; margin-bottom:4px; text-transform:uppercase;">Lesson 5</span>
